 OPTIONS_HELP.txt    |  34 ++++++++++++-
 src/gles/present.rs |  38 +++++++++++++-
 src/options.rs      |  72 +++++++++++++++++++++-----
 src/window.rs       | 121 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 4 files changed, 214 insertions(+), 51 deletions(-)

diff --git a/OPTIONS_HELP.txt b/OPTIONS_HELP.txt
index 1651ec4..c1b6866 100644
--- a/OPTIONS_HELP.txt
+++ b/OPTIONS_HELP.txt
@@ -122,8 +122,8 @@ Game controller options:
         part of the screen.
 
         This is three parts separated by commas: the name of a button (DPadLeft,
-        DPadUp, DPadRight, DPadDown, Start, LeftShoulder or Xbox-like
-        A, B, X or Y), the X co-ordinate and the Y co-ordinate.
+        DPadUp, DPadRight, DPadDown, Start, LeftShoulder, RightShoulder or
+        Xbox-like A, B, X or Y), the X co-ordinate and the Y co-ordinate.
         The co-ordinates are floating-point (decimal) numbers. 0,0 is the
         top-left corner. The bottom-right corner is 320,480 if the app is in
         portrait, and 480,320 if the app is in landscape.
@@ -197,6 +197,36 @@ Game controller options:
         such that sharp movements take about half a second to complete, while
         movements within a 10px radius will be completely ignored.
 
+    --virtual-cursor-relative=...
+        Make the analog stick move the virtual cursor like a mouse, instead of
+        pointing it at a spot on the screen. The cursor stays where you leave it
+        and is always shown.
+
+        The value is how many screen widths the cursor travels per second with
+        the stick pushed all the way.
+
+    --virtual-cursor-stick=...
+        Which analog stick controls the virtual cursor: "left" or "right". The
+        default is right. Pressing that stick or the shoulder button on the
+        same side taps, unless --virtual-cursor-button= is given.
+
+    --virtual-cursor-button=...
+        A button that taps with the virtual cursor, for example A, instead of
+        the stick and shoulder button, which are then free for
+        --button-to-touch=. This takes the same button names as
+        --button-to-touch=.
+
+    --virtual-cursor-dpad
+        With --virtual-cursor-relative=, the D-pad also moves the cursor, at a
+        steady speed a little below the stick's.
+
+    --virtual-cursor-arrow=...
+        Draw the virtual cursor as an arrow pointer in this color, with its tip
+        on the point it touches, instead of a small square. It is lighter while
+        pressed.
+
+        The value is a color as six hexadecimal digits, for example e0201c.
+
 Graphics driver options:
     --gles1=...
         Force touchHLE to use a particular OpenGL ES 1.1 implementation.
